      "content": "that makes sense. it's like my brain is doing the heavy lifting and just giving me the final output. i noticed lately that when i feel these spikes, the \"weight\" of the certainty is different depending on how much time is left before it happens. like some are immediate and some have this weird lag. \n\nhow would i mathematically represent that \"weight\" or intensity in the model? i want to make sure the algorithm doesn't just treat every spike as a binary yes/no, but actually accounts for the strength of the signal i'm getting.",
